{"ts": 1794666708.5200858, "tool": "write_file", "args": {"Content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <limits.h>\n\nstatic void printLine(const char *line)\n{\n    if (line != NULL)\n    {\n        puts(line);\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void printHexCharLine(char charHex)\n{\n    printf(\"%02x\\n\", charHex);\n}\n\nstatic void goodG2B(void)\n{\n    char data;\n    data = ' ';\n    data = -2;\n    {\n        char result = (char)(data - 1);\n        printHexCharLine(result);\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void goodB2G(void)\n{\n    char data;\n    data = ' ';\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%c\", &data);\n    if (data > CHAR_MIN)\n    {\n        char result = (char)(data - 1);\n        printHexCharLine(result);\n    }\n    else\n    {\n        printLine(\"data value is too large to perform subtraction.\");\n    }\n}\n\nvoid good(void)\n{\n    goodG2B();\n    goodB2G();\n}\n\nvoid bad(void)\n{\n    char data;\n    data = ' ';\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%c\", &data);\n    {\n        char result = (char)(data - 1);\n        printHexCharLine(result);\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[])\n{\n    const char *mode = (argc > 1) ? argv[1] : \"both\";\n\n    if (strcmp(mode, \"bad\") != 0)\n    {\n        printLine(\"Calling good()...\");\n        good();\n        printLine(\"Finished good()\");\n    }\n    if (strcmp(mode, \"good\") != 0)\n    {\n        printLine(\"Calling bad()...\");\n        bad();\n        printLine(\"Finished bad()\");\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n", "Overwrite": true, "Path": "/tmp/run_a62bb424e5f5431a96810e87832042b1/reconstructed.c"}, "decision": "allow", "reason": null}
